# Never use `bmod`

**Do not run `bmod` under any circumstances.** On DTU LSF it is **admin-only** (`bsub error: Only administrators can run bmod!`) and will always fail for student accounts.

This applies to the agent **and** to advice given to the user — do not suggest `bmod` as a fix.

## Change queue, walltime, or resources

1. **`bkill <JOBID>`** — only when the user explicitly asks to cancel or move/resubmit a job.
2. Set the correct queue in the **submit script** (`#BSUB -q gpuv100`, etc.) or inline `bsub` heredoc.
3. **`bsub`** again (or `bash hpc/submit/...`) to get a new JOBID.

Example (move PEND job from `gpua100` → `gpuv100`):

```bash
bkill <JOBID>
bash hpc/submit/cv4fold/submit_ablation_incohort_followup.sh   # script already uses gpuv100
# or resubmit a single job with #BSUB -q gpuv100
```

## Allowed LSF job commands

| Command | Agent may use when |
|---------|-------------------|
| `bjobs`, `bhist`, `tail` | Checking status (snapshot only) |
| `bsub` | User explicitly confirmed submit |
| `bkill` | User explicitly asked to cancel or resubmit/move |
| **`bmod`** | **Never** |

See also: [hpc-bsub-communication.mdc](hpc-bsub-communication.mdc), [hpc-gpu-queue-split.mdc](hpc-gpu-queue-split.mdc).
